A45 — run on Vulkan 1.1 drivers

The Arm drivers on the Pixel 7 (Mali-G710 r36p0, 1.1.201), the Pixel 6 and the
Galaxy A34 (Mali-G78 and Mali-G68 r32p1, 1.1.177) report apiVersion 1.1, so
selectPhysDev skipped them and gamescope exited with "failed to find physical
device". Those drivers ship most of the 1.2 features as extensions.

A 1.1 device is now accepted. On it the device is created with the extension
feature structures instead of VkPhysicalDeviceVulkan12Features and 13Features:
VK_KHR_timeline_semaphore and VK_EXT_scalar_block_layout (both required, with
an error naming the missing one), VK_KHR_shader_float16_int8 (else the fp32
FSR and NIS shaders), VK_KHR_image_format_list when present (else DRM format
modifiers are turned off, since the modifier extension needs it on 1.1), and
VK_KHR_dynamic_rendering with its create_renderpass2 and depth_stencil_resolve
dependencies (else ReShade effects are not loaded). The timeline and dynamic
rendering entry points are loaded by their KHR names. The device-limits log
reads the same values from the extension structures.

VK_EXT_robustness2 is optional on every device. Without nullDescriptor, empty
descriptor slots get 1x1 zero placeholders (2D RGBA8 sampled and storage, 1D
and 3D RGBA16 for the LUTs, and a 2x2 NV12 image with the YCbCr conversion
for the immutable-sampler slots, or the 2D placeholder in the A44 fallback
layout). On the swapchain backends VK_KHR_swapchain_mutable_format,
VK_KHR_present_id and VK_KHR_present_wait are optional: without the first the
swapchain is created with one view format, without the others presents carry
no id and the present-wait thread is not started. Each missing extension logs
one "<extension> not available, ..." line.

A 1.2 or newer device with these extensions takes the same extensions, the same
feature chain and the same code paths as before.

